---
title: Styleguide
layout: base.njk
description: Current UI patterns and component reference for the DLF Forum 2026 site.
permalink: /styleguide/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---

{% set colorTokens = [
    { name: 'Primary', token: '--color-primary', use: 'Primary actions, active navigation, editorial emphasis' },
    { name: 'Primary Container', token: '--color-primary-container', use: 'Full-bleed page heroes and deep brand panels' },
    { name: 'Primary Fixed', token: '--color-primary-fixed', use: 'Icon tiles and quiet brand accents inside cards' },
    { name: 'Accent', token: '--color-accent', use: 'Warm emphasis, supporting highlights, and small moments of contrast' },
    { name: 'Surface', token: '--color-surface', use: 'Page background and navigation glass' },
    { name: 'Surface Low', token: '--color-surface-container-low', use: 'Alternating section bands on long-form pages' },
    { name: 'Surface Highest', token: '--color-surface-container-highest', use: 'Dense cards and stronger content containers' },
    { name: 'Outline Variant', token: '--color-outline-variant', use: 'Soft borders, dividers, timelines, and embedded frames' },
    { name: 'Info Soft', token: '--color-info-soft', use: 'Informational callouts and support messaging' },
    { name: 'Success Soft', token: '--color-success-soft', use: 'Confirmed and completed states' }
] %}

{% set typeScale = [
    { label: 'Display Hero', class: 'font-headline text-[3.4rem] md:text-[5.2rem] font-extrabold leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.045em]', text: 'Call for Proposals' },
    { label: 'Landing Hero', class: 'font-headline text-[3.25rem] md:text-[4.35rem] leading-[1.04] tracking-[-0.045em]', text: 'Welcome to the Virtual DLF Forum' },
    { label: 'Section Title', class: 'section-title', text: 'Reusable page rhythm' },
    { label: 'Card Heading', class: 'font-headline text-[1.75rem] font-extrabold leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em]', text: 'A broad practitioner mix' },
    { label: 'Body', class: 'text-lg leading-8 text-on-surface-variant', text: 'Forum pages use generous line height, clear hierarchy, and warm paper-like contrast for long-form guidance.' },
    { label: 'Eyebrow', class: 'eyebrow', text: 'DLF Forum 2026' },
    { label: 'Mono Label', class: 'font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-variant', text: 'Phase 01 / Oct 14-15' }
] %}

{% set timeline = [
    { phase: 'Phase 01', title: 'Submissions Open', date: 'April 14, 2026', active: true },
    { phase: 'Phase 02', title: 'CFP Deadline', date: 'May 11, 2026', active: false },
    { phase: 'Phase 03', title: 'Forum Dates', date: 'October 14-15, 2026', active: false }
] %}

{% set refinements = [
    { number: '01', title: 'Glass Navigation', text: 'The primary nav now floats above the page with a translucent surface, stronger hierarchy, and a cleaner mobile menu.' },
    { number: '02', title: 'Editorial Hero System', text: 'Page intros use either a split landing hero or a full-bleed image hero with direct action and restrained supporting copy.' },
    { number: '03', title: 'Section Chips', text: 'Long pages use compact chip links so readers can jump between sections without adding another heavy sidebar pattern.' },
    { number: '04', title: 'Elevated Resource Cards', text: 'Resource and archive links use a lighter, more polished card treatment with subtle lift on hover.' }
] %}

<div class="styleguide-shell">
    <section class="relative overflow-hidden px-8 pt-40 pb-24">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl editorial-grid items-center">
            <div class="col-span-12 z-10 lg:col-span-7">
                <p class="eyebrow">Design Reference</p>
                <h1 class="mt-4 font-headline text-5xl font-extrabold leading-none tracking-tight text-on-surface md:text-7xl">
                    Forum 2026 UI.
                </h1>
                <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
                    The active site language is more editorial and more structured: floating navigation, sharper hero treatments, chip-based section routing, softer elevated cards, and clearer action placement across long pages.
                </p>
                <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
                    <a href="#refinements" class="button-primary">Review refinements</a>
                    <a href="#components" class="button-secondary">View components</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="col-span-12 mt-12 lg:col-span-5 lg:mt-0">
                <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-4xl bg-primary text-on-primary shadow-2xl">
                    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-linear-to-br from-primary via-primary-container/90 to-info/80"></div>
                    <div class="relative p-10 md:p-12">
                        <p class="font-label text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-on-primary/90">System Snapshot</p>
                        <h2 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-bold leading-tight">
                            Build pages as clear editorial sections with a distinct next step.
                        </h2>
                        <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
                            <div class="rounded-3xl border border-on-primary/15 bg-on-primary/12 p-5 backdrop-blur-sm">
                                <p class="font-headline text-xl font-bold">Context first</p>
                                <p class="mt-1 text-on-primary">Lead with the page purpose before asking readers to act.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="rounded-3xl border border-on-primary/15 bg-on-primary/12 p-5 backdrop-blur-sm">
                                <p class="font-headline text-xl font-bold">Navigation stays light</p>
                                <p class="mt-1 text-on-primary">Use chips, timelines, and cards to keep long pages scannable.</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="rounded-3xl border border-on-primary/15 bg-on-primary/12 p-5 backdrop-blur-sm">
                                <p class="font-headline text-xl font-bold">Surfaces feel warm</p>
                                <p class="mt-1 text-on-primary">Prefer paper-toned backgrounds, soft borders, and restrained motion.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="refinements" class="border-y border-outline-variant/30 bg-surface-container-low">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-8 py-20">
            <div class="max-w-3xl">
                <p class="eyebrow">Refinements</p>
                <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">UI Patterns</h2>
                <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
                    These are the patterns the pages now rely on most heavily. New work should follow these treatments before introducing anything bespoke.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
                {% for item in refinements %}
                    <article class="surface-card p-8">
                        <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-variant">{{ item.number }}</span>
                        <h3 class="mt-4 font-headline text-2xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">{{ item.title }}</h3>
                        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">{{ item.text }}</p>
                    </article>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="flow" class="px-8 py-20">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
            <div class="max-w-3xl">
                <p class="eyebrow">Page Flow</p>
                <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">The current rhythm</h2>
                <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
                    Start with a concise hero, introduce page-specific context, use chips or cards to break up long content, and close with a direct action or practical next step instead of generic promotional copy.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-4">
                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-variant">01</span>
                    <h3 class="mt-4 font-headline text-2xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Hero</h3>
                    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">Use either a split editorial intro for landing pages or a full-width image hero for focused content pages.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-variant">02</span>
                    <h3 class="mt-4 font-headline text-2xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Orientation</h3>
                    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">Introduce the page scope early with a short note, chips, badges, or a compact contextual block.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-variant">03</span>
                    <h3 class="mt-4 font-headline text-2xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Scannable Body</h3>
                    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">Alternate open sections and low-contrast bands to keep dense guidance pages readable.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-variant">04</span>
                    <h3 class="mt-4 font-headline text-2xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Action</h3>
                    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">End sections with a button, resource link, or date marker that helps the reader move forward immediately.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="tokens" class="border-y border-outline-variant/30 bg-surface-container-low">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-8 py-20">
            <div class="max-w-3xl">
                <p class="eyebrow">Tokens</p>
                <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Color and type</h2>
                <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
                    Shared tokens come from the Tailwind theme in <code class="font-mono text-sm">site.css</code>. Reuse these values and the existing typography utilities instead of introducing page-specific color systems.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-10 grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
                {% for swatch in colorTokens %}
                    <article class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-outline-variant/30 bg-surface-container-lowest shadow-(--shadow-card)">
                        <div class="h-28" style="background: var({{ swatch.token }});"></div>
                        <div class="p-5">
                            <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">{{ swatch.name }}</h3>
                            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs font-semibold text-on-surface-variant">{{ swatch.token }}</p>
                            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">{{ swatch.use }}</p>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>

            <div class="mt-12 space-y-5">
                {% for type in typeScale %}
                    <article class="surface-card p-6 md:p-8">
                        <div class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-[12rem_minmax(0,1fr)] md:items-center">
                            <div>
                                <p class="font-label text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">{{ type.label }}</p>
                                <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-on-surface-variant">{{ type.class }}</p>
                            </div>
                            <p class="{{ type.class }}">{{ type.text }}</p>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section id="components" class="px-8 py-20">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
            <div class="max-w-3xl">
                <p class="eyebrow">Components</p>
                <h2 class="mt-3 section-title">Current reusable patterns</h2>
                <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
                    These examples match the active site language now used across the homepage, resources, and call for proposals pages.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-10 showcase-grid">
                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <p class="eyebrow">Navigation</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Floating glass shell</h3>
                    <div class="glass-nav mt-6 rounded-[1.6rem] border border-outline-variant/30 bg-surface/80 p-5 shadow-[0_8px_32px_rgba(70,119,194,0.06)]">
                        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4">
                            <span class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-primary-fixed-variant">DLF Forum 2026</span>
                            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-5 text-sm">
                                <span class="border-b-4 border-primary/40 pb-1 font-headline font-bold text-on-primary-fixed-variant">Home</span>
                                <span class="font-headline font-bold text-on-surface/70">Call for Proposals</span>
                                <span class="font-headline font-bold text-on-surface/70">Resources</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
                        Use the fixed glass treatment for site-level navigation only. Keep page-level orientation lighter with chips or inline anchors.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="surface-card overflow-hidden p-0">
                    <div class="page-hero relative min-h-[22rem] bg-primary-container">
                        <div class="absolute inset-0">
                            <div class="page-hero-overlay absolute inset-0"></div>
                            <img alt="" class="h-full w-full object-cover" src="/static/compare-fibre-fRGoTJFQAHM-unsplash.webp">
                        </div>
                        <div class="page-hero-inner relative z-10 px-8 text-center">
                            <p class="eyebrow !text-white/90">Page Hero</p>
                            <h3 class="mt-4 font-headline text-[2.8rem] font-extrabold leading-[0.98] tracking-[-0.045em] text-on-primary md:text-[3.5rem]">Call for Proposals</h3>
                            <p class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-7 text-on-primary/84 md:text-lg">
                                Use the full-bleed hero for high-priority program pages that need stronger framing and a clear first action.
                            </p>
                            <div class="page-hero-actions mt-8 flex flex-col justify-center gap-4 sm:flex-row">
                                <a class="button-primary" href="#0">Submit Your Proposal</a>
                                <a class="button-secondary border-white/25 bg-white/10 text-white hover:bg-white/16 hover:text-white" href="#0">Learn More</a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <p class="eyebrow">Section Navigation</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Anchor chips</h3>
                    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                        <a href="#0" class="chip-link">Accessibility</a>
                        <a href="#0" class="chip-link">Topics of Interest</a>
                        <a href="#0" class="chip-link">Session Formats</a>
                        <a href="#0" class="chip-link">Important Dates</a>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
                        Use these on long single-page documents when readers need fast section jumps without the visual weight of a sidebar.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <p class="eyebrow">Actions</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Buttons and inline links</h3>
                    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
                        <a href="#0" class="button-primary">Register for the Forum</a>
                        <a href="#0" class="button-secondary">Explore the program</a>
                        <a href="#0" class="button-ghost">
                            Read the Code of Conduct
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-base" aria-hidden="true">arrow_outward</span>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-on-surface-variant">
                        Use <a href="#0" class="text-link">inline links</a> when the action belongs inside editorial copy rather than as a standalone decision.
                    </p>
                </article>

                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <p class="eyebrow">Cards</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Resource card</h3>
                    <a class="resource-card mt-6 block p-8" href="#0">
                        <div class="flex h-full flex-col">
                            <div class="mb-8 flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
                                <span class="inline-flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-primary-fixed text-primary">
                                    <span class="material-symbols-outlined" aria-hidden="true">article</span>
                                </span>
                                <span class="font-mono text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-variant">01</span>
                            </div>
                            <h4 class="font-headline text-[1.9rem] leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-on-surface">For presenters</h4>
                            <p class="mt-5 flex-1 leading-8 text-on-surface-variant">Guidance, planning materials, and practical support for Forum contributors.</p>
                            <span class="mt-10 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-label text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-primary">
                                Open resource
                                <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-base" aria-hidden="true">arrow_forward</span>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                    </a>
                </article>

                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <p class="eyebrow">Content Cards</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Feature and fact patterns</h3>
                    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4">
                        <div class="rounded-[1.75rem] bg-secondary-fixed p-6">
                            <h4 class="font-headline text-[1.5rem] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-on-secondary-fixed">A broad practitioner mix</h4>
                            <p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-on-secondary-fixed-variant">Use colored fact cards sparingly for high-value summaries on landing pages.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="surface-card rounded-[1.75rem] p-6 shadow-none">
                            <h4 class="font-headline text-[1.35rem] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.025em] text-on-surface">Participatory</h4>
                            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-on-surface-variant">Default to the neutral card when repeating structured guidance across sections.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <p class="eyebrow">Forms</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Inputs</h3>
                    <div class="mt-6 space-y-5">
                        <div>
                            <label class="form-label" for="sg-name">Full name</label>
                            <input id="sg-name" class="form-field" type="text" placeholder="Jordan Lee">
                        </div>
                        <div>
                            <label class="form-label" for="sg-topic">Session topic</label>
                            <select id="sg-topic" class="form-field">
                                <option>Choose a track</option>
                                <option>Collections and Stewardship</option>
                                <option>Community and Advocacy</option>
                                <option>Infrastructure</option>
                            </select>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <p class="eyebrow">Callouts</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Status messaging</h3>
                    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4">
                        <div class="callout callout-info">
                            <p class="font-label text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Informational</p>
                            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">Use for deadline reminders, support guidance, and registration updates that need to stay visible.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="callout callout-success">
                            <p class="font-label text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Success</p>
                            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">Use for confirmed submissions, completed forms, and post-action feedback.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <p class="eyebrow">Timeline</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Important dates</h3>
                    <div class="mt-8">
                        {% for item in timeline %}
                            <div class="relative border-l-2 border-outline-variant pb-10 pl-8 last:border-l-0 last:pb-0">
                                <div class="absolute -left-2.25 top-0 h-4 w-4 rounded-full ring-4 ring-surface-container-lowest {% if item.active %}bg-primary{% else %}bg-secondary-container{% endif %}"></div>
                                <span class="font-headline text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider {% if item.active %}text-primary{% else %}text-secondary{% endif %}">{{ item.phase }}</span>
                                <h4 class="mt-1 font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface">{{ item.title }}</h4>
                                <p class="mt-2 text-on-surface-variant">{{ item.date }}</p>
                            </div>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="surface-card p-8">
                    <p class="eyebrow">Utilities</p>
                    <h3 class="mt-3 font-headline text-3xl font-extrabold text-on-surface">Small but persistent behaviors</h3>
                    <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-on-surface-variant">
                        <p class="leading-relaxed">Use the skip link and the floating scroll-to-top button as shared accessibility and navigation utilities rather than page-specific features.</p>
                        <p class="leading-relaxed">Keep smooth scrolling and anchor offsets aligned with the fixed navigation so section links land cleanly below the header.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
                        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-primary/10 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-primary">
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-base" aria-hidden="true">arrow_upward</span>
                            Scroll to top
                        </span>
                        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-tertiary-fixed px-4 py-2 text-sm font-bold text-on-tertiary-fixed">
                            <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-base" aria-hidden="true">keyboard_tab</span>
                            Skip link
                        </span>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>
